  <data name="Onboarding_Title1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Scan hardware and ownership</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Onboarding_Body1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Start with a read-only inventory of devices, control evidence, user-session bridges, and competing hardware owners. This step cannot change hardware state.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Onboarding_Title2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Know what RigPilot can control</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Onboarding_Body2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Verified controls have apply, read-back, and reset evidence. Experimental controls require explicit confirmation. Read-only and blocked endpoints remain visible with their exact evidence gap or conflict.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Onboarding_Title3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Choose a daily mode</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Onboarding_Body3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Quiet reduces background power, Efficiency favours useful work per watt, and Performance favours responsiveness without automatic voltage increases. Selection alone never writes hardware.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Onboarding_Title4" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Measure the baseline</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Onboarding_Body4" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Capture three read-only telemetry samples so the result has a before-state. Missing sensors are reported as missing instead of being estimated.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Onboarding_Title5" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Review eligibility and omissions</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Onboarding_Body5" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The dry run lists the exact action that can be applied and why optional cooling, tuning, or lighting actions are omitted. Commissioning and Advanced Lab steps remain opt-in.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Onboarding_Title6" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Apply one verified transaction</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Onboarding_Body6" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The service prepares the prior state, applies the eligible mode action, reads it back, and commits only after verification. A failed apply enters verified rollback or Recovery Required.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Onboarding_Title7" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Review proof and restoration</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Onboarding_Body7" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Review the transaction proof. You can independently restore the Windows Balanced default and require a successful default-state read-back before setup is complete.</value>
  </data>
